clk: qcom: dispcc-sm6115: Stop the display AHB clock holding the XO on

The DSI PHY holds the display's AHB clock prepared for as long as it's
bound, and that clock's parent is the XO, so the CPUs never vote the XO off
in system sleep. QCM2290 solves this by using the active-only XO, and this
does the same.

The binding and the driver both keep old device trees working, and that
fallback was tried: without the new clock the parent is the regular XO as
before.

The SoC as a whole still doesn't reach XO shutdown with this, as the ADSP
doesn't go idle on this phone. It only removes the CPUs' vote from the
picture.

Only tested on a Moto G Power (2021), with Plasma Mobile and kmscube.
